<div class="tool-comparison-grid">
  <article class="tool-comparison-card tool-comparison-card--featured">
    <h3>Giskard OSS</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>Dynamic scan</dt><dd><a href="/oss/scan/explanation/how-scan-works">Target-aware scenarios</a>, generated and judged from a description or knowledge base</dd>
      <dt>Structured agents</dt><dd><a href="/oss/checks/explanation/core-concepts">Serializable inputs and outputs</a>, plus <a href="/oss/scan/how-to/wrap-your-agent">declared Pydantic input schemas</a></dd>
      <dt>Multi-agent and multi-turn</dt><dd><a href="/oss/checks/tutorials/multi-turn">Stateful scenarios</a>; test a multi-agent system by <a href="/oss/scan/how-to/wrap-your-agent">wrapping the whole system</a></dd>
      <dt>Quality evaluation</dt><dd>Deterministic and LLM-graded <a href="/oss/checks/explanation/when-to-use-which-check">Checks</a>, plus knowledge-base-driven <code>quality_scan</code></dd>
      <dt>Red teaming</dt><dd><a href="/oss/solutions/scan-vulnerabilities"><code>vulnerability_scan</code></a> tailors attacks to the target</dd>
      <dt>pytest</dt><dd><a href="/oss/checks/how-to/run-in-pytest">Native async pytest tests</a> with <code>pytest-asyncio</code></dd>
    </dl>
  </article>

  <article class="tool-comparison-card">
    <h3>garak</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>Dynamic scan</dt><dd>Configurable <a href="https://docs.garak.ai/garak/garak-components/vulnerability-probes">probe catalog</a>, including adaptive <a href="https://docs.garak.ai/garak/automatic-red-teaming/garaks-auto-red-team">auto red-team probes</a></dd>
      <dt>Structured agents</dt><dd><a href="https://docs.garak.ai/garak/garak-components/using-generators">Generator interfaces</a>, primarily for text-generation targets</dd>
      <dt>Multi-agent and multi-turn</dt><dd>Some probes use <a href="https://docs.garak.ai/garak/automatic-red-teaming/garaks-auto-red-team">multiple turns</a></dd>
      <dt>Quality evaluation</dt><dd>Primarily an <a href="https://docs.garak.ai/garak">LLM vulnerability scanner</a></dd>
      <dt>Red teaming</dt><dd>Core workflow for probing models and systems for <a href="https://docs.garak.ai/garak">vulnerabilities</a></dd>
      <dt>pytest</dt><dd>No first-class workflow documented</dd>
    </dl>
  </article>

  <article class="tool-comparison-card">
    <h3>promptfoo</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>Dynamic scan</dt><dd><a href="https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/red-team/quickstart/">Generates red-team tests</a> from purpose, plugins, and strategies</dd>
      <dt>Structured agents</dt><dd>Configurable <a href="https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/providers/">providers</a>, including HTTP endpoints and custom code</dd>
      <dt>Multi-agent and multi-turn</dt><dd><a href="https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/red-team/strategies/">Strategies</a> include multi-turn attacks</dd>
      <dt>Quality evaluation</dt><dd>Configurable <a href="https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/configuration/expected-outputs/">assertions and metrics</a></dd>
      <dt>Red teaming</dt><dd>Core workflow using <a href="https://www.promptfoo.dev/docs/red-team/">plugins and strategies</a></dd>
      <dt>pytest</dt><dd>CI integrations documented; pytest is not the native runner</dd>
    </dl>
  </article>

  <article class="tool-comparison-card">
    <h3>PyRIT</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>Dynamic scan</dt><dd>Programmable <a href="https://azure.github.io/PyRIT/">attacks and executors</a> against configured targets</dd>
      <dt>Structured agents</dt><dd>Attacks and executors connect to <a href="https://azure.github.io/PyRIT/">prompt targets</a>, including HTTP targets</dd>
      <dt>Multi-agent and multi-turn</dt><dd><a href="https://azure.github.io/PyRIT/">Multi-turn attacks</a> execute against targets</dd>
      <dt>Quality evaluation</dt><dd>Reusable <a href="https://azure.github.io/PyRIT/">scorers</a> for attack outcomes and response properties</dd>
      <dt>Red teaming</dt><dd>Core workflow for building and running <a href="https://azure.github.io/PyRIT/">attacks with executors</a></dd>
      <dt>pytest</dt><dd>No first-class workflow documented</dd>
    </dl>
  </article>

  <article class="tool-comparison-card">
    <h3>DeepEval + DeepTeam</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>Dynamic scan</dt><dd><a href="https://deepeval.com/docs/red-teaming-introduction">DeepTeam generates attacks</a> from vulnerabilities and enhancements</dd>
      <dt>Structured agents</dt><dd><a href="https://deepeval.com/docs/red-teaming-introduction#model-callback">Model callbacks</a> for DeepTeam; structured test cases for DeepEval</dd>
      <dt>Multi-agent and multi-turn</dt><dd><a href="https://deepeval.com/docs/metrics-conversation-completeness">Conversational metrics</a> in DeepEval; multi-turn attacks in DeepTeam</dd>
      <dt>Quality evaluation</dt><dd>Extensible <a href="https://deepeval.com/docs/metrics-introduction">evaluation metrics</a></dd>
      <dt>Red teaming</dt><dd><a href="https://deepeval.com/docs/red-teaming-introduction">DeepTeam</a> handles red teaming; DeepEval supplies metrics</dd>
      <dt>pytest</dt><dd><a href="https://deepeval.com/docs/evaluation-test-cases">Evaluation test cases with pytest</a> through <code>deepeval test run</code></dd>
    </dl>
  </article>
</div>

